Thought: I should use a chemistry tool to help analyze this reaction. The [2+2] photocycloaddition between a cyclopentenone and allene would likely produce bicyclic products. I need to determine which of the given SMILES represents the major product.
Action: chemistry_tool
Action Input: {"query": "Predict the major and minor products of the photochemical [2+2] cycloaddition between CC(C)C1=CC(CC1)=O (a cyclopentenone with isopropyl group) and C=C=C (allene) under irradiation in dichloromethane at -78 deg C. Compare with the given options: A. C=C1C[C@@]([C@H]21)(C(C)C)CCC2=O is the major product and O=C1C2C(C(C2)=C)(C(C)C)CC1 the minor product. B. O=C1C2C(C(C2)=C)(C(C)C)CC1 is the major product and C=C1C[C@@]([C@H]21)(C(C)C)CCC2=O the minor product."}
